  "version": "2.5.1",
  "notes": "A fix for confirmations, which didn't stop anything in 2.5.0. Update if you use the desktop app.\n\n- Desktop: **Fixed: confirmations didn't stop anything in the installed app (2.5.0 and earlier).** On macOS, Windows and Linux the \"Are you sure?\" questions never appeared and every action went ahead as if you had said OK: deleting files or snapshots, reboot, snapshot restore, Re-enable all, Optimize's Run plan, display scaling, uninstall and the rest. They now open a native dialog, and Cancel cancels. Naming a snapshot uses the app's own dialog, so Save snapshot and the Launcher's \"Save snapshot first\" work on macOS, where they did nothing.\n- Linux AppImage: updating in the app works. Each AppImage was repacked after it was signed, so since in-app updates arrived in 2.0.0-beta.14 the app rejected every AppImage update as having an invalid signature and stayed on its version. The release now signs the repacked file and checks every update signature before publishing, so an AppImage from 2.0.0-beta.14 through 2.5.0 can update to this version in the app.\n\n### First-run warnings\n\nThese builds are unsigned. Your OS may complain on first launch:\n\n- **macOS** (Gatekeeper): the first-launch dialog on macOS 15+ only offers \"Move to Trash\" or \"Done\" — click **Done**, then either:\n    - **Terminal:** `xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine \"/Applications/ATV Optimizer.app\"` (one-time, then double-click as normal)\n    - **GUI:** System Settings → Privacy & Security → scroll to the \"ATV Optimizer was blocked\" message → **Open Anyway** → enter password\n- **macOS** (Local Network): click **Allow** when macOS asks to find devices on your local network. If no TV is found, click **Restart ADB**. If that doesn't help, open System Settings → Privacy & Security → Local Network, turn ATV Optimizer off and on again (every entry, if it's listed more than once), then click **Restart ADB** again.\n- **Windows** (SmartScreen): \"More info\" → \"Run anyway\".\n- **Linux**: `chmod +x ATV.Optimizer*.AppImage` before running.\n\nSee the [README](https://github.com/bryanroscoe/shield_optimizer#readme) for setup and feature docs.",
